<div class="post-container">

  <h1 class="post-title">The Truth About Meniscectomy</h1>
  <div class="post-meta">Published: May 25, 2026 · 3 min read</div>

  <div class="post-content">

    <p><strong>Here is what they don’t tell you about meniscectomy.</strong></p>

    <p><strong>Knee swelling:</strong> Even after the procedure, swelling can linger longer than most people expect. It’s normal, but it can be frustrating if you’re trying to get back to activity quickly.</p>

    <p><strong>There is still pain afterwards:</strong> A meniscectomy removes the damaged tissue, but it doesn’t magically erase the irritation inside the joint. Some discomfort is common during the early phases of recovery.</p>

  </div>

